                                        "entry_id": "4fcb8acc-95cd-3865-91db-c20aa4d232f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With malaria; where people may catch malaria."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a place or region"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b6117a9-ff3b-4526-9202-11e8bbfa6923",
                                                "sense_id": "6a9fc96a-14ae-39c6-9f82-98d7c2bea6c6",
                                                "text": "In spite of quinine, the men sickened day by day. Many of them, fine, strong, active fellows, who had never known what a day's sickness meant, went down before the malarious mist that gathered in the jungles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4e7cd85-71ef-4658-ad61-249e871eb410",
                                                "sense_id": "6a9fc96a-14ae-39c6-9f82-98d7c2bea6c6",
                                                "text": "Dr. Abrams, the Columbia expert, said in an interview that the Uganda findings had additional implications for treating H.I.V.-infected children in malarious areas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
